1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,678
RelayGuard turns Mezo MUSD into paid orders and paid API access.

2
00:00:03,678 --> 00:00:06,353
A seller needs more than a token balance.

3
00:00:06,353 --> 00:00:11,368
They need to know which order was paid, by whom, and for exactly how much.

4
00:00:11,368 --> 00:00:15,890
A merchant verifies a receiving wallet and shares an invoice link or QR.

5
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:19,716
The buyer reviews the amount and signs a direct MUSD transfer.

6
00:00:19,716 --> 00:00:25,281
RelayGuard marks the invoice paid only when the receipt matches the token, payer, merchant, and amount.

7
00:00:25,281 --> 00:00:27,715
The merchant keeps their wallet and storefront.

8
00:00:27,715 --> 00:00:32,449
For software agents, the merchant protects an Express API route with x402.

9
00:00:32,449 --> 00:00:35,604
An unpaid request returns exact MUSD payment terms.

10
00:00:35,604 --> 00:00:37,576
The buyer signs an authorization.

11
00:00:37,576 --> 00:00:41,126
The facilitator settles before the middleware releases the response.

12
00:00:41,126 --> 00:00:45,465
Any required Permit Two approval is limited to the requested amount.

13
00:00:45,465 --> 00:00:48,701
Mezo is also part of the treasury policy.

14
00:00:48,701 --> 00:00:53,152
RelayGuard reads Trove Manager and Price Feed at one pinned block.

15
00:00:53,152 --> 00:00:56,793
At one hundred eighty percent collateralization, configured limits apply.

16
00:00:56,793 --> 00:01:02,052
At one hundred twenty five percent, every positive MUSD payment needs human review.

17
00:01:02,052 --> 00:01:06,098
Below Mezo's one hundred ten percent minimum, spending is blocked.

18
00:01:06,098 --> 00:01:08,930
If protocol reads fail, MUSD authorization pauses.

19
00:01:08,930 --> 00:01:13,380
These controlled examples run the actual policy functions without sending funds.

20
00:01:13,380 --> 00:01:19,615
Wave Two includes merchant-owned destinations, configurable paid routes, wallet preflight, and auditable protocol evidence.

21
00:01:19,615 --> 00:01:28,077
This revision adds explicit operator permissions, signed buyer sessions, retry after wallet rejection, and recovery after an interrupted submission.

22
00:01:28,077 --> 00:01:32,530
Both historical Testnet payment paths were rechecked against Mezo RPC.

23
00:01:32,530 --> 00:01:36,539
This video uses current product captures and historical receipts.

24
00:01:36,539 --> 00:01:41,649
Our first customers are API sellers and digital merchants already using MUSD.

25
00:01:41,649 --> 00:01:47,186
Next, three design partners will test setup time, payment completion, and repeat use.

26
00:01:47,186 --> 00:01:51,019
A nineteen-dollar monthly operations tier is a pricing hypothesis.

27
00:01:51,019 --> 00:01:54,000
RelayGuard makes MUSD usable, and payments accountable.
